, "contents": [{"type": "pdf", "content": "engenn9le04ob05re7pdf01.pdf"}]}]}], "type": "DWS", "id": 11, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " \nResearch Emotional Intelligence.\n"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Take Away"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment."}]}]}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn9le04ob05re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn9le04ob05re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn9le04ob05re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn9le04ob05re2img01.jpg", "text": "So, I've been having a few problems at work lately. I asked myself what I could do about it. A friend told me I had to learn more about managing my emotions. I had heard the term emotional intelligence and decided to find out more about it.  I should have read about it before now because it is very interesting to me. Having this information last week could have helped me with my interactions with my boss.", "id": 1}, {"time": "21500", "image": "engenn9le04ob05re2img02.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Emotional Intelligence (EI)</span> describes the ability to recognize your own and other people's emotions, to differentiate between different feelings and label them appropriately, and to use emotional information to guide thinking and behavior.\nStudies have shown that people with high EI have greater mental health, exemplary job performance, and more potent leadership skills. If you have emotional intelligence you can understand the emotions of other people.", "id": 2}, {"time": "48000", "image": "engenn9le04ob05re2img03.jpg", "text": "A co-worker told me I needed to learn to communicate clearly and manage conflict.  I probably would have coped better with stress at work if I had been more familiar with EI. Apparently it's possible to boost your EI level. A higher EI can improve your performance at work. It can help you navigate the social complexities of the workplace, lead and motivate others and excel in your career. People at work said that I could be more productive if I could communicate better. I should have done this research a long time ago!", "id": 3}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}]}]}